      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2021-november/q2",
      "question": "<p>The cubic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"9x^3-5x^2+4x+7=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\gamma\"></span>.</p><p>Without solving the equation, find the cubic equation whose roots are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3\\alpha-2)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3\\beta-2)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3\\gamma-2)\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"aw^3+bw^2+cw+d=0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are integers to be determined.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
