      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2021-november/q6",
      "question": "<p>A mining company has identified a mineral layer below ground.</p><p>The mining company wishes to drill down to reach the mineral layer and models the situation as follows.</p><p>With respect to a fixed origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>,</p><ul><li>the ground is modelled as a horizontal plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=0\"></span></li><li>the mineral layer is modelled as part of the plane containing the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(10,5,-50)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(15,30,-45)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-5,20,-60)\"></span>, where the units are in metres</li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Determine an equation for the plane containing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\mathbf n=d\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Determine, according to the model, the acute angle between the ground and the plane containing the mineral layer. Give your answer to the nearest degree. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The mining company plans to drill vertically downwards from the point (5, 12, 0) on the ground to reach the mineral layer.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li>Using the model, determine, in metres to 1 decimal place, the distance the mining company will need to drill in order to reach the mineral layer. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>State a limitation of the assumption that the mineral layer can be modelled as a plane. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
