      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2021-november/q8",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Prove by induction that, for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r(r+1)(2r+1)=\\frac{1}{2}n(n+1)^2(n+2)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Hence, show that, for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=n}^{2n}r(r+1)(2r+1)=\\frac{1}{2}n(n+1)(an+b)(cn+d)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are integers to be determined.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
